   "subject": "Output - df, SE, CV",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Dear distance samplers<div><br></div><div>I concluded my analysis some ago, yet looking at some of the results now, I get slightly confused.</div><div>Especially regarding how to present my findings.</div><div><br></div><div>1. Why does df for many of my results have two decimals? - do you just remove the decimals, rounding the number?</div><div><br></div><div>2. The CV seems to be calculated form the SE. Is that statistically allowed? - when CV is usually calculated from SD</div><div><br></div><div>3. Do you write your results as density +- SE and abundance +- SE? - or is it better to use the 95%CI in parenthesis after the results?</div><div><br></div><div>4. Do reviewers prefer to have encounter rate and such included in the results section, or are density and abundance results usually enough? - the article is not a methods article.</div><div><br></div><div>Thank you in advance for your help.</div><div>Malene</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
